<title>HONG KONG: Shougang Int'l 1996 net down 45 percent.</title>
<headline>Shougang Int'l 1996 net down 45 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	6.5	vs  12.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents) 1.0	vs  2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil	vs  19.33 gain</p>
<p>    Net			 100.39   vs  185.32</p>
<p>    Turnover		  5,658.50 vs  7,304.52</p>
<p>    Company name	    Shougang Concord International</p>
<p>				  Enterprises Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close	     June 10-12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	July 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Shougang Concord International engages in trading of steel products and construction materials, transportation and shipping, metals processing and property investment. It also makes steel, electrical and electronic products, ferrous and non-ferrous metals, and minerals.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs 3.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
